# Windows batch files and script hosts must use CRLF line endings.
#
# cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files once they grow: an 8KB LF-only
# deploy_env.bat had its REM/echo lines executed as commands from
# arbitrary byte offsets, while the smaller LF-only scripts happened to
# survive. Keep *.bat / *.cmd / *.vbs checked out as CRLF everywhere so a
# clone, a USB copy and the working tree all behave identically.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
